Objectives

• Represent a courier hub and service areas as vertices in a graph.
• Represent roads and their distances as weighted edges.
• Implement Dijkstra’s shortest-path algorithm using C++.
• Calculate the shortest delivery distance from the hub to every reachable service area.
• Identify and display service areas that cannot be reached from the hub.
• Demonstrate a practical use of gralgorithms in courier and delivery management.
